Sval: hide Firefox's tab-strip settings and its session restore

about:preferences' Tabs interaction fieldset acts only on Firefox's tab strip,
which Sval's workspace panel replaces; Sval locks each pref, which hides the
controls but not the fieldset heading. "Open previous windows and tabs" is
always on in Sval, which reopens every window of the last session with its
workspace (Sval spec §10.4). Appearance's "Customize browser layout"
link opens the browser layout group, which Sval's locks hide. None of these
has a pref of its own that hides it, so the setting config is the only lever.

diff --git a/browser/components/preferences/config/appearance.mjs b/browser/components/preferences/config/appearance.mjs
index 6a2a200d7f..d06f6ee6f4 100644
--- a/browser/components/preferences/config/appearance.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/preferences/config/appearance.mjs
@@ -86,6 +86,9 @@ Preferences.addSetting({
 
 Preferences.addSetting({
   id: "related-settings-tabs-browsing-link",
+  // Sval: the link opens Firefox's browser layout (horizontal or vertical
+  // tabs), which Sval locks off for its workspace panel.
+  visible: () => false,
   onUserClick: e => {
     e.preventDefault();
     window.gotoPref("paneTabsBrowsing-layout");
